  "section_notes": "The final S2 sets a 5% failure threshold that triggers only a corrective-action plan and retest, with no sales stop, which protects Northwind's Hearth 10 at 6.2%. S5 makes a recall mandatory above 8 per 100,000 with no transition or corrective alternative, which exposes Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9. S3's six-year retrofit window favours Northwind, whose installed base has only 38% shut-off capability."
